  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Initial Request**: User asked to modify the `AppIcon.vue` component to display a \"file\" icon when the app is a file viewer, instead of the default project icon or hamburger menu.\n\n2. **File Context Provided**: Three Vue components were provided as context: `AppIcon.vue` (the target component), `FileViewer.vue` (file viewing component), and `TabManager.vue` (tab management component).\n\n3. **Component Structure**: User specified Vue component structure requirements including the need for `<script setup>`, `<template>`, and `<script>` sections with no CSS (TailwindCSS only) and no ref/computed imports.\n\n4. **Solution Implemented**: Added an `isFileViewer` computed property to detect file viewer apps and modified the template to conditionally render a file icon (`fa-regular fa-file`) with proper icon priority hierarchy.\n\n5. **Clarification Note**: The solution uses `app.name` or `app.id` properties to identify file viewers, with a note requesting confirmation of the exact identifier if different values are used in the actual application.",
